-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1068: a nested rule written left of the outer rule's
-- clauses, which hang right of PARTY. Its LEST, written at its own clauses,
-- is its own. The first version of the fix gave it to the outer rule, so the
-- trace below blamed Buyer for the Seller's missed delivery.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Seller, Buyer, Carrier
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF delivery, payment, collection

hanging MEANS
  PARTY Seller
      MUST delivery
      WITHIN 3
      HENCE
    PARTY Buyer
    MUST payment
    WITHIN 7
    LEST BREACH BY Buyer

-- The Seller never delivers; an unrelated event on day 10 shows the miss.
#TRACE hanging AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Carrier DOES collection AT 10
